.TH CAD-WINE-LAUNCHER 1 "October 2026" "cad-wine-launcher 0.2.0"
.SH NAME
cad-wine-launcher \- Community CAD Launcher for Autodesk Fusion
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cad-wine-launcher
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ -- " application arguments" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs a user-supplied Autodesk Fusion installer in a private Wine prefix and
launches the installed application. Autodesk Fusion is not included or
downloaded by this package. The launcher is unofficial and unaffiliated with
Autodesk, Inc. The user must accept Autodesk's terms and have a valid entitlement.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --install
Install without launching Fusion.
.TP
.BI --installer " PATH"
Use an installer obtained directly by the user from Autodesk.
.TP
.B --accept-autodesk-terms
Confirm non-interactively that Autodesk's terms were reviewed and accepted and
that the user has a valid entitlement.
.TP
.B --update
Update Fusion with a user-selected Autodesk installer.
.TP
.B --status
Report installation status without making changes.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Print configured paths and download sources without making changes.
.TP
.B --debug
Show application output and Wine diagnostics.
.TP
.B --help
Show usage.
.SH FILES
Data and logs are stored beneath the XDG data directory in cad-wine-launcher.
Downloads are stored beneath the XDG cache directory in cad-wine-launcher.
Flatpak redirects these directories into its private application storage.
The host directory ~/.autodesk_fusion is mapped to Wine drive H: for model
exchange and is intentionally outside the Flatpak's private application data.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Status exits zero when installed and one otherwise. Setup exits zero when
installation files are present and one on failure. Launches preserve the
Wine process exit status. This does not verify CAD operation.
